Spoilers...






















> Is it where you drop some objects
>such as leather armor and stuff and keep zapping them with a wand of 
>polymorph until you get something useful? I tried it and I must have zapped
>a little to much because I felt "shuddering vibrations" and the thing 
>disappeared.

You have the basic idea right.  Usually, polypiling involves making a
fairly large pile of stuff and zapping a wand of polymorph at it.
This gives you many polymorphed items per charge of the wand.  Then,
you go over to the pile, take out the items you like, and try again.

Warning:  Polypiling can have bad side effects.  The most common is
the one you noticed--sometimes the pile will shudder and some of the
objects will simply disappear.  By far the most dangerous, however, is
that piles containing many metal objects have a chance of coalescing
into an iron golem.  Iron golems are not terribly difficult for very
tough characters, but they will easily destroy most low-level
characters.  So if you polypile before you're strong, you are taking a
big risk.

(BTW, does anyone know if piles of other materials have a chance of
forming other kinds of golems?  It's not as frightening a possibility,
since most golems aren't nearly as tough as the iron ones).


